cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both papers listed under
  "references" below: the 2022 Computational Materials Science paper for
  the cohesive-energy and planar-fault statistics, and the Baski et al.
  manuscript for the short-range-order, vacancy formation, and vacancy
  migration statistics. The Baski et al. entry will be updated with journal,
  volume, pages, and DOI when the article is published.
title: Solid-Solution-PE-Statistics
abstract: >-
  Analytical calculation of the statistical distributions (mean and standard
  deviation) of cohesive energies, vacancy formation and migration energies,
  and generalized planar fault energies in concentrated FCC solid solutions
  described by embedded-atom-method potentials, for random alloys and for
  alloys with Warren-Cowley short-range order.
